<title>EGYPT: Average yield falls on Egyptian T-bills.</title>
<headline>Average yield falls on Egyptian T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 8.956 percent at Monday's auction from 9.950 percent at the previous auction on June 2.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 1,382.475 million pounds, replace bills worth 970.550 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 1.2 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):.</p>
<p>Maturity date: Dec 9, 1997 (Dec 2, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.956 percent (9.950)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,382.475 million (1,444.925 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,666.775 million (1,644.925 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.500-9.031 percent (8.500-9.450)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.500-9.935 percent (8.500-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 91 (180)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 141 (180)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
